<!--
  Audio, without an engine.

  WHY THIS EXISTS. CircleAI.Voice holds two different things under one name: the
  primitives every audio path needs - a sample format, a microphone interface, a
  speaker interface, WAV, a level-based VAD, a transcript - and the ENGINES that
  turn audio into words and words into audio: Whisper, the ONNX TTS voices, the
  Zipformer keyword spotter.

  The engines bring Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime and Whisper.net.Runtime with them,
  and NuGet native assets are not optional for a consumer: referencing the
  assembly for AudioFormat put libonnxruntime.so (18.3 MB) and five whisper
  libraries into an app that only wanted to open the microphone and send the
  bytes somewhere else. It was 18 MB of an engine nothing in that process could
  call, and no reference the app declared said so.

  So the primitives moved down here and CircleAI.Voice references them. THE
  NAMESPACE IS STILL CircleAI.Voice - deliberately. A namespace is not an
  assembly: every `using CircleAI.Voice;` in the tree keeps compiling, no call
  site changes, and the only thing that moved is which .dll a type is in. The
  same trick made CircleAIService possible.

  NOTHING IN HERE MAY REFERENCE AN ENGINE. That is the whole contract. If a type
  here needs Whisper or ONNX, it belongs in CircleAI.Voice, not in this project -
  and a PackageReference added here would silently undo the split.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <RootNamespace>CircleAI.Voice</RootNamespace>
    <PackageId>CircleAI.Audio</PackageId>
    <Description>The engine-free half of CircleAI's voice stack: sample formats, microphone and speaker contracts, WAV, level-based voice activity detection, transcripts and subtitles. Carries no inference runtime, so a client can capture and play audio without shipping ONNX Runtime or Whisper.</Description>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
